These solvers form the physical foundation of the Chronos‑State Engine.

2.2 Chaos and Bifurcation Theory

Chaotic systems exhibit sensitivity to initial conditions, leading to divergent trajectories even under small perturbations. Bifurcation theory describes transitions between stable and unstable dynamical regimes. The Chronos‑State Engine applies these principles to planetary systems by embedding chaotic evolution within the simulation pipeline.

